 "readme": "College values as data.json stores them, mapped to the name to print. The raw value stays the matching key everywhere: cohort keys, factoid ids and the tool's own filter are unchanged, and only the text a reader sees comes from this file. Read by scripts/factoids.py and reusable by the prerender script. A value with no entry here prints as it is stored.",
 "rules": [
  "A standalone \" St\" is a truncated \"State\". \"St.\" with a full stop is Saint and is left alone, so St. John's stays St. John's.",
